Customer Churn Analysis Using Python

1. Introduction

Customer churn is one of the biggest challenges faced by subscription-based businesses. Understanding customer behavior helps organizations improve customer satisfaction and increase revenue. This project performs a complete end-to-end business analysis using Python.

2. Business Problem

The company is experiencing customer churn, resulting in decreased revenue and customer lifetime value. The objective is to identify the reasons behind customer churn and recommend effective retention strategies.

3. Objectives
Analyze customer data.
Identify churn patterns.
Perform statistical analysis.
Generate meaningful visualizations.
Provide business recommendations.
4. Dataset Description

Dataset Name: Customer Churn Dataset

Number of Records: 500

Data Cleaning Performed:

Duplicate removal
Missing value checking
Data type conversion
Label Encoding
5. Technologies Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Scikit-learn
Google Colab
6. Data Cleaning

The dataset was inspected for missing values and duplicate records. Categorical variables were converted into numerical values using Label Encoding for analysis.

7. Exploratory Data Analysis

Performed:

Descriptive Statistics
Correlation Analysis
Distribution Analysis
Customer Segmentation
Churn Analysis

Visualizations:

Pie Chart
Histogram
Bar Chart
Box Plot
Scatter Plot
Correlation Heatmap
8. Key Findings
Customers with higher monthly charges showed higher churn rates.
Customers with shorter tenure were more likely to leave.
Long-term customers demonstrated stronger loyalty.
Monthly charges and tenure significantly influenced customer retention.
9. Business Recommendations
Launch customer loyalty programs.
Provide personalized offers.
Improve customer onboarding.
Monitor high-risk customer segments.
Reduce churn using predictive analytics.
10. Conclusion

The project successfully completed the entire business analysis workflow from raw data to actionable business insights. The findings can help organizations make informed business decisions and improve customer retention.
